e":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproduceable 4.8.dev4\nNot reproduceable 4.8.dev3\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev4 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors (1920x1080 @ 60.00 Hz, 2560x1440 @ 59.95 Hz) - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1050 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8266) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-6700 CPU @ 3.40GHz (8 threads) - 15.94 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen editing a gdscript file with one of the methods highlighted in the method list panel, if you pause typing then the text cursor will jump to the first line of the highlighted function name. If a method name is not highlighted then pausing typing does not affect the cursor position.\n\nIn 4.8.dev3 pausing the typing removed the highlight from the method list and did not reposition the cursor.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n<img width=\"1269\" height=\"569\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5fea821b-9ec0-44ce-b267-a9f8bc0849fb\" />\n\n- Create a new script file with several methods\n- Click/Highlight one of the methods in the method list, _process in this example\n- Click anywhere in the script and type a few characters\n- When typing is paused for more than about 1 second the cursor will jump to the first line of the highlighted method, line 10 in this example\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev","html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/followers","following_url":"h